@* Nothing to show, and what to do about it.

   The app said this four different ways — a bare .empty, a .hits-empty, a .head with a .call
   inside it, and plain alerts. An empty list is not a problem to be announced, so this is quiet
   markup rather than a notice, but it should always answer the same two questions: what is missing,
   and what fills it. *@

<div class="empty-state">
    <p class="what">@ChildContent</p>
    @if (Action is not null)
    {
        <div class="act">@Action</div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What is missing, in the user's terms.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The control that fills it, when there is one.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Action { get; set; }
}
